        "id": "ch6_3-1",
        "text": "Using ConvertTo- and Export- cmdlets\nIf we want our PowerShell objects in a format other than text, we\u2019re going to need to process them\nsomehow. There are two groups of cmdlets that let us do that. The ConvertTo- cmdlets convert the\nobjects in our pipeline into data of a particular type, such as CSV or HTML data. The Export- cmdlets\ncombine the equivalent ConvertTo- cmdlet with an Out-File function to produce a file of the\nrelevant type. In this chapter, we\u2019re going to cover three common file types; CSV, XML, and HTML.\nUsing ConvertTo- and Export- cmdlets\n147\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 CSV\n\u2022 XML\n\u2022 HTML\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
